    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0345" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg305"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 916.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 6, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the reception of
                    despatches from the department numbered from 1303 to 1316, inclusive.</p>
                <p>With regard to the directions contained in Nos. 1309, 1311, and 1315, as well as
                    1294, previously received, I had obtained an opportunity for an interview with
                    Lord Russell to talk over the matters contained in them on Tuesday last; but
                    upon paying my visit, I found his lordship was so unwell as to be unable to see
                    me. I then left with him the despatches, as he had suggested, for his
                    information only; and I made an arrangement to wait upon him as soon as he
                    should be prepared to assign me a day.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
